{"version":1,"settings":{"newPerDay":30,"reviewLimit":60,"fetchLongman":true,"againMinutes":10,"efMax":2.8,"hardFactor":1.2,"easyFactor":1.3,"autoMasterDays":0},"words":[{"id":"wmvs5wywmw0f7l","term":"situate","key":"situate","userDef":"义：使位于；使处于某种背景或环境中。常用被动 be situated in/on/at。例：The town is situated at the junction of three provinces.（小镇位于三省交界处）也可说 situate a story in the 1930s，把故事设定在 20 世纪 30 年代。","createdAt":1793194851766,"srs":{"ef":2.6,"interval":4,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793548800000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793240443995,"history":[{"t":1793240443995,"grade":5,"ivl":4,"ef":2.6}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793240443995},{"id":"wmvs5wywm4s4t8","term":"junction","key":"junction","userDef":"义：交汇处；交叉点；连接处。搭配：at the junction of A and B。例：at the junction of three provinces 位于三省交界处。也可指道路、铁路的交汇点。","createdAt":1793194851767,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793240571753,"history":[{"t":1793240571753,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793240571753},{"id":"wmvs5wywm37nj7","term":"converge","key":"converge","userDef":"义：汇聚；交会；趋于一致。搭配：converge at/on。例：The three borders converge here.（三条边界在此交会）抽象用法：Their opinions converged. 意见趋于一致。","createdAt":1793194851768,"srs":{"ef":2.46,"interval":8,"reps":2,"lapses":0,"due":1793980800000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793321794338,"history":[{"t":1793240929901,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36},{"t":1793321794338,"grade":5,"ivl":8,"ef":2.46}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793321794338},{"id":"wmvs5wywm5sqw2","term":"glisten","key":"glisten","userDef":"义：闪亮；泛着微光，常因水分、湿润表面或光线反射而发亮。搭配：glistening water / a glistening river。常有湿润、清亮的视觉效果。","createdAt":1793194851769,"srs":{"ef":2.46,"interval":8,"reps":2,"lapses":0,"due":1793980800000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793321867703,"history":[{"t":1793241035331,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36},{"t":1793321867703,"grade":5,"ivl":8,"ef":2.46}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793321867703},{"id":"wmvs5wywmc0rve","term":"glitter","key":"glitter","userDef":"义：闪闪发光；闪耀，通常突出许多明亮、醒目的光点。例：The stars glittered in the sky.（星星在天空中闪烁）也可指浮华、表面光鲜：the glitter of fame。","createdAt":1793194851770,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":6,"reps":2,"lapses":0,"due":1793808000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793322214322,"history":[{"t":1793241334236,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36},{"t":1793322214322,"grade":4,"ivl":6,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793322214322},{"id":"wmvs5wywm1emof","term":"glow","key":"glow","userDef":"义：发出柔和、持续的光；泛红；容光焕发。例：glow in the dark；the sky glowed red。辨：相比 glitter，通常不是许多尖锐的闪光点，而是较柔和、连续的光。","createdAt":1793194851771,"srs":{"ef":2.22,"interval":3,"reps":2,"lapses":0,"due":1793548800000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793322284514,"history":[{"t":1793241608478,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36},{"t":1793322284514,"grade":3,"ivl":3,"ef":2.22}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793322284514},{"id":"wmvs5wywmmjq4a","term":"idyllic","key":"idyllic","userDef":"义：田园诗般的；宁静美好的；理想化的。搭配：an idyllic village / an idyllic setting。辨：比 peaceful 更有理想化、如诗如画的意味。","createdAt":1793194851772,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":6,"reps":2,"lapses":0,"due":1793808000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793322484232,"history":[{"t":1793241836544,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36},{"t":1793322484232,"grade":4,"ivl":6,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793322484232},{"id":"wmvs5wywm99dgc","term":"a border town","key":"a border town","userDef":"义：边境小镇；边界地区的城镇。搭配：a remote border town 偏远的边陲小镇。注意拼写是 border，不是 boder。","createdAt":1793194851773,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":6,"reps":2,"lapses":0,"due":1793808000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793322501202,"history":[{"t":1793242294342,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36},{"t":1793322501202,"grade":4,"ivl":6,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793322501202},{"id":"wmvs5wywmd34cp","term":"wind its way through","key":"wind its way through","userDef":"义：蜿蜒穿过；曲折延伸穿过。例：A stream winds its way through the town.（一条小溪蜿蜒穿过小镇）辨：wind 在这里读 /waɪnd/，不是“风”的 /wɪnd/。","createdAt":1793194851774,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793242534662,"history":[{"t":1793242534662,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793242534662},{"id":"wmvs5wywmt7vxd","term":"wind its way along","key":"wind its way along","userDef":"义：沿着……蜿蜒延伸。例：The path winds its way along the river.（小路沿河蜿蜒延伸）辨：through 强调穿过某区域；along 强调沿着某条线或某个边缘延伸。","createdAt":1793194851775,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793242552645,"history":[{"t":1793242552645,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793242552645},{"id":"wmvs5wywmuedz8","term":"ferry","key":"ferry","userDef":"义：渡船；渡运服务；渡运。可作名词或动词：take the ferry 乘渡船；ferry passengers across the river 把乘客渡送到河对岸。","createdAt":1793194851776,"srs":{"ef":2.6,"interval":4,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793548800000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793242673883,"history":[{"t":1793242673883,"grade":5,"ivl":4,"ef":2.6}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793242673883},{"id":"wmvs5wywm33n47","term":"ferryboat","key":"ferryboat","userDef":"义：渡船，尤指用于运送乘客或车辆横渡水域的船。辨：与 ferry 意义重叠，但 ferry 更灵活，也能指整个渡运服务；普通行文中往往不必特意用 ferryboat。","createdAt":1793194851777,"srs":{"ef":2.6,"interval":4,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793548800000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793242684119,"history":[{"t":1793242684119,"grade":5,"ivl":4,"ef":2.6}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793242684119},{"id":"wmvs5wywmkhz8x","term":"ferryman","key":"ferryman","userDef":"义：摆渡人；渡船船夫。传统语境中常指负责操船、把人渡过河的人。","createdAt":1793194851778,"srs":{"ef":2.6,"interval":4,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793548800000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793242695894,"history":[{"t":1793242695894,"grade":5,"ivl":4,"ef":2.6}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793242695894},{"id":"wmvs5wywmbrq57","term":"boatman","key":"boatman","userDef":"义：船夫；操船的人。辨：范围比 ferryman 广，不一定专门从事摆渡。","createdAt":1793194851779,"srs":{"ef":1.96,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":1,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793244130088,"history":[{"t":1793242827191,"grade":1,"ivl":0,"ef":1.96},{"t":1793244130088,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":1.96}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793244130088},{"id":"wmvs5wywmv8bv3","term":"tend","key":"tend","userDef":"义：照料；看管；料理；照管。搭配：tend a garden / tend livestock / tend the ferry。辨：tend the ferry 可以表示看管渡船，但不一定明确表示实际操船。","createdAt":1793194851780,"srs":{"ef":2.22,"interval":3,"reps":2,"lapses":0,"due":1793548800000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793322523678,"history":[{"t":1793243880118,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36},{"t":1793322523678,"grade":3,"ivl":3,"ef":2.22}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793322523678},{"id":"wmvs5wywm4oulj","term":"ply","key":"ply","userDef":"义：定期往返；在固定航线上运营；从事某种活动。例：Ferries ply between the two banks.（渡船往返于两岸）强调规律性、持续性的运输活动。","createdAt":1793194851781,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":6,"reps":2,"lapses":0,"due":1793808000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793322643425,"history":[{"t":1793244114187,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36},{"t":1793322643425,"grade":4,"ivl":6,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793322643425},{"id":"wmvs5wywm9vejr","term":"shuttle","key":"shuttle","userDef":"义：在两地之间往返运送；穿梭。例：The boat shuttles passengers between the two banks.（小船往返于两岸运送乘客）强调反复接送。","createdAt":1793194851782,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":6,"reps":2,"lapses":0,"due":1793808000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793323207233,"history":[{"t":1793244213142,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36},{"t":1793323207233,"grade":4,"ivl":6,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793323207233},{"id":"wmvs5wywma4i9z","term":"glide","key":"glide","userDef":"义：平稳、轻柔地滑行。例：The ferry glided across the river.（渡船平稳地滑过河面）突出运动的流畅、轻盈，而不是固定航线。","createdAt":1793194851783,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793244363013,"history":[{"t":1793244363013,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793244363013},{"id":"wmvs5wywmriee3","term":"undercurrent","key":"undercurrent","userDef":"义：暗流；潜流；潜在的情绪、趋势或影响。搭配：an undercurrent beneath the surface 表面之下的暗流。比喻用法：an undercurrent of tension 潜藏的紧张气氛。","createdAt":1793194851784,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793244479372,"history":[{"t":1793244479372,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793244479372},{"id":"wmvs5wywm1sbtm","term":"stealthy","key":"stealthy","userDef":"义：秘密的；悄无声息的；不易察觉的。搭配：a stealthy movement / a stealthy approach。强调行动隐蔽，常带有谨慎、秘密甚至鬼祟的意味。","createdAt":1793194851785,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793244604941,"history":[{"t":1793244604941,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793244604941},{"id":"wmvs5wywm9g85e","term":"stir","key":"stir","userDef":"义：搅动；微微移动；激起情绪或反应。例：The wind stirred the leaves.（风吹动了树叶）stir emotions 激起情绪。也可指某种力量开始活动：Something was stirring beneath the surface。","createdAt":1793194851786,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793244819192,"history":[{"t":1793244819192,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793244819192},{"id":"wmvs5wywm85n5k","term":"stir up","key":"stir up","userDef":"义：搅起；激起；挑起；煽动。搭配：stir up trouble / anger / controversy 惹起麻烦、激起愤怒、引发争议。辨：比单独的 stir 更常强调引发某种反应或使局势变得不平静。","createdAt":1793194851787,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793244871578,"history":[{"t":1793244871578,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793244871578},{"id":"wmvs5wywm0xim1","term":"move","key":"move","userDef":"此义 = progress。义：发展；推进；演变；运行。例：Events are moving quickly.（事态进展很快）History moves on. 历史继续向前发展。辨：Fate moves beneath the surface 是文学性的拟人表达，不是 move = progress 在所有语境中都能互换。","createdAt":1793194851788,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793244927706,"history":[{"t":1793244927706,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793244927706},{"id":"wmvs5wywml6fnb","term":"woodland sprite","key":"woodland sprite","userDef":"义：林间精灵；森林中的小精灵。sprite 指精灵、仙灵，常用于奇幻或文学语境。例：a girl as free-spirited as a woodland sprite（一个像林间精灵般自由灵动的女孩）","createdAt":1793194851789,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793244983128,"history":[{"t":1793244983128,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793244983128},{"id":"wmvs5wywmq6vwd","term":"forthright","key":"forthright","userDef":"义：直率的；坦诚的；直截了当的。搭配：a forthright person / a forthright manner。强调说话、表达态度时坦率直接，通常是正面评价。","createdAt":1793194851790,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793245017297,"history":[{"t":1793245017297,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245017297},{"id":"wmvs5wywmcl2bd","term":"hearty","key":"hearty","userDef":"义：热情友好的；爽朗的；衷心的；丰盛的。搭配：a hearty welcome / hearty laughter / a hearty meal。辨：形容人时可指热情、爽朗，但不等于“豪爽”的全部含义。","createdAt":1793194851791,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245052254,"history":[{"t":1793245052254,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245052254},{"id":"wmvs5wywmet9mn","term":"vivacity","key":"vivacity","userDef":"义：活泼；生气勃勃；充满活力。搭配：her vivacity and charm（她的活泼与魅力）强调生命力、活力和生动感。","createdAt":1793194851792,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245107801,"history":[{"t":1793245107801,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245107801},{"id":"wmvs5wywmne5ur","term":"alacrity","key":"alacrity","userDef":"义：欣然；敏捷积极；乐意而迅速的反应。搭配：respond with alacrity 欣然迅速地回应。辨：强调做事时的积极、爽快和乐意，不直接等于“灵动”。","createdAt":1793194851793,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245156346,"history":[{"t":1793245156346,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245156346},{"id":"wmvs5wywml6c0m","term":"duel","key":"duel","userDef":"义：决斗；对决；竞争。搭配：a duel between the two brothers（两兄弟之间的对决）传统上可指武力决斗，也可比喻激烈竞争。","createdAt":1793194851794,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245198445,"history":[{"t":1793245198445,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245198445},{"id":"wmvs5wywme0h9j","term":"duet","key":"duet","userDef":"义：二重奏；二重唱；两人合作表演。搭配：sing a duet 唱二重唱。辨：与 duel 只差一个字母，但 duel 强调对抗，duet 强调两人共同演奏或演唱。","createdAt":1793194851795,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793245206766,"history":[{"t":1793245206766,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245206766},{"id":"wmvs5wywm9lo0y","term":"smart from","key":"smart from","userDef":"义：因……而感到痛苦、愤愤不平。搭配：smart from rejection 因遭到拒绝而痛苦。更常见的搭配还包括 smart under criticism（因受到批评而难受）、smart with humiliation（因受辱而痛苦）","createdAt":1793194851796,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245379561,"history":[{"t":1793245379561,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245379561},{"id":"wmvs5wywma0kfm","term":"courtship","key":"courtship","userDef":"义：求爱；追求某人的过程；求婚前的恋爱交往。搭配：the courtship of a young woman（追求一位年轻女性）辨：语体比 dating 正式、传统，常见于文学或历史叙述。","createdAt":1793194851797,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245415858,"history":[{"t":1793245415858,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245415858},{"id":"wmvs5wywmx8dqv","term":"pale into insignificance","key":"pale into insignificance","userDef":"义：相形见绌；显得微不足道。例：All other concerns paled into insignificance beside this loss.（与这次损失相比，其他事情都显得微不足道）辨：这里的 pale 是“显得黯淡”，不是身体变苍白。","createdAt":1793194851798,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245603155,"history":[{"t":1793245603155,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245603155},{"id":"wmvs5wywmoner3","term":"despondent","key":"despondent","userDef":"义：沮丧的；失去希望的；意气消沉的。搭配：feel / become despondent。辨：比一般的 sad 更强调失去信心、看不到希望。","createdAt":1793194851799,"srs":{"ef":2.6,"interval":4,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793548800000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793245646297,"history":[{"t":1793245646297,"grade":5,"ivl":4,"ef":2.6}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245646297},{"id":"wmvs5wywm6ek4p","term":"lose one's heart to someone","key":"lose one's heart to someone","userDef":"义：爱上某人；倾心于某人。例：Both brothers lose their hearts to Cuicui.（两兄弟都爱上了翠翠）辨：比 fall in love with 更有文学色彩。","createdAt":1793194851800,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245662132,"history":[{"t":1793245662132,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245662132},{"id":"wmvs5wywm9walx","term":"ringing","key":"ringing","userDef":"义：清脆响亮的；嘹亮的；回响的。搭配：a ringing voice 响亮清晰的声音。也可表示斩钉截铁的：a ringing endorsement（明确有力的支持）","createdAt":1793194851801,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245744559,"history":[{"t":1793245744559,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245744559},{"id":"wmvs5wywmkkppc","term":"resonate","key":"resonate","userDef":"义：回响；产生共鸣；引起共鸣。例：His words resonated with the audience.（他的话引起了听众的共鸣）也可指声音在空间中回荡。","createdAt":1793194851802,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793245821419,"history":[{"t":1793245821419,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245821419},{"id":"wmvs5wywmguixk","term":"resonant","key":"resonant","userDef":"义：洪亮的；共鸣的；引起共鸣的。搭配：a deep, resonant voice 低沉浑厚的声音。辨：它是形容词；resonate 是动词。","createdAt":1793194851803,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793245850661,"history":[{"t":1793245850661,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245850661},{"id":"wmvs5wywmvnofi","term":"drown","key":"drown","userDef":"义：溺水；淹死；淹没、压过声音。搭配：drown in the river 在河中溺亡；drown out the noise 压过噪声。注意：drown 本身不表示自杀。","createdAt":1793194851804,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245879741,"history":[{"t":1793245879741,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245879741},{"id":"wmvs5wywmdi4oz","term":"elect","key":"elect","userDef":"义：选择；决定（较正式）。搭配：elect to leave town 选择离开小镇。辨：比 choose to 正式，常用于较书面或强调自主选择的语境。","createdAt":1793194851805,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245930959,"history":[{"t":1793245930959,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245930959},{"id":"wmvs5wywmebaar","term":"insurmountable","key":"insurmountable","userDef":"义：无法逾越的；无法克服的。搭配：an insurmountable obstacle / barrier。既可指物理障碍，也可指抽象困难，侧重“无法跨越或克服”。","createdAt":1793194851806,"srs":{"ef":2.6,"interval":4,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793548800000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793245944269,"history":[{"t":1793245944269,"grade":5,"ivl":4,"ef":2.6}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245944269},{"id":"wmvs5wywm21tb2","term":"insuperable","key":"insuperable","userDef":"义：无法克服的；难以逾越的。搭配：an insuperable difficulty / obstacle。辨：与 insurmountable 意义相近，但更正式、书面。","createdAt":1793194851807,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793245968201,"history":[{"t":1793245968201,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793245968201},{"id":"wmvs5wywmtfok2","term":"surmount","key":"surmount","userDef":"义：越过；克服；战胜。搭配：surmount an obstacle / difficulty 越过障碍、克服困难。既可用于物理意义，也可用于抽象意义。","createdAt":1793194851808,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793246024980,"history":[{"t":1793246024980,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246024980},{"id":"wmvs5wywml4rn0","term":"sturdy","key":"sturdy","userDef":"义：结实的；强健的；坚固耐用的。搭配：a sturdy man / sturdy legs / a sturdy bridge。强调力量、坚固和耐用，不一定意味着体型粗壮。","createdAt":1793194851809,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793246067166,"history":[{"t":1793246067166,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246067166},{"id":"wmvs5wywma4tci","term":"stocky","key":"stocky","userDef":"义：矮壮的；敦实的。搭配：a stocky man（一个身材矮壮的男人）主要描述体型，通常意味着身材较矮、躯干宽厚。","createdAt":1793194851810,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793246078625,"history":[{"t":1793246078625,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246078625},{"id":"wmvs5wywmswp4r","term":"pagoda","key":"pagoda","userDef":"义：佛塔；塔式宗教建筑。搭配：a white pagoda（一座白塔）用于中国传统建筑时通常译作“塔”，但具体建筑类型仍需结合实际形制。","createdAt":1793194851811,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793246090274,"history":[{"t":1793246090274,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246090274},{"id":"wmvs5wywmtelle","term":"crumple","key":"crumple","userDef":"义：弄皱；压瘪；因失去支撑而瘫倒、蜷缩。搭配：crumple a piece of paper 把纸揉皱；He crumpled to the ground.（他瘫倒在地）辨：一般不用于描述一座塔整体倒塌。","createdAt":1793194851812,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793246154036,"history":[{"t":1793246154036,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246154036},{"id":"wmvs5wywmrvm1f","term":"guardian","key":"guardian","userDef":"义：守护者；监护人。搭配：a legal guardian 法定监护人；a guardian of the child 孩子的守护者。可以指法律身份，也可以指实际保护者。","createdAt":1793194851813,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793246172019,"history":[{"t":1793246172019,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246172019},{"id":"wmvs5wywm98847","term":"misgiving","key":"misgiving","userDef":"义：疑虑；顾虑；不安的预感。搭配：have misgivings about something（对某事心存疑虑）通常指对某个决定、计划或可能发生的事情感到不安。","createdAt":1793194851814,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793246189957,"history":[{"t":1793246189957,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246189957},{"id":"wmvs5wywmddaed","term":"pine for","key":"pine for","userDef":"义：深切思念；苦苦渴望。搭配：pine for home / a lost love / a better life。强调长期、深切的思念或渴望，往往带有痛苦意味。","createdAt":1793194851815,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793246240996,"history":[{"t":1793246240996,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246240996},{"id":"wmvs5wywmfcskk","term":"interminable","key":"interminable","userDef":"义：仿佛没有尽头的；漫长得令人难以忍受的。搭配：an interminable wait / an interminable meeting。不仅强调时间长，还常带有主观上的煎熬或厌倦。","createdAt":1793194851816,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793376000000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793246274365,"history":[{"t":1793246274365,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246274365},{"id":"wmvs5wywmtu6zg","term":"watch over","key":"watch over","userDef":"义：照看；守护；保护。搭配：watch over a child 照看孩子。辨：强调持续关注和保护，比 look at 或 watch 更有照料意味。","createdAt":1793194851817,"srs":{"ef":2.36,"interval":1,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793289600000,"lastGrade":3,"lastReview":1793246296289,"history":[{"t":1793246296289,"grade":3,"ivl":1,"ef":2.36}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246296289},{"id":"wmvs5wywm0g5lp","term":"lifelong","key":"lifelong","userDef":"义：终身的；持续一生的。搭配：a lifelong friend / a lifelong commitment。辨：通常作定语修饰名词；表示某个动作持续一生时，常用 all one's life 或 throughout one's life。","createdAt":1793194851818,"srs":{"ef":2.6,"interval":4,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793548800000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793246307145,"history":[{"t":1793246307145,"grade":5,"ivl":4,"ef":2.6}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793246307145},{"id":"wmvtf6wcain2bi","term":"deny","key":"deny","userDef":"义：否认；拒绝给予。核心是不承认某事属实，或不允许某人获得某物。搭配：deny doing sth.（否认做过某事）、deny that...（否认……）、deny sb. sth.（拒绝给予某人某物）、deny a request（拒绝请求）。例：He denied stealing the money.（他否认偷了钱）She denied that she had made a mistake.（她否认自己犯了错）They denied him access to the building.（他们不让他进入大楼）常见搭配：deny responsibility 否认责任、deny access 拒绝进入、deny the existence of sth. 否认某事物的存在。音：/dɪˈnaɪ/ v.","createdAt":1793270897722,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":2,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793462400000,"lastGrade":4,"lastReview":1793322438119,"history":[{"t":1793322438119,"grade":4,"ivl":2,"ef":2.5}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793322438119},{"id":"wmvtf6wca3fvog","term":"sophisticated","key":"sophisticated","userDef":"义：复杂精密的；见多识广的；老练的。关键不是简单的「高级」，而是具有复杂性、精细性，或成熟的判断力。搭配：sophisticated technology 精密技术；a sophisticated analysis 深入而复杂的分析；a sophisticated audience 有鉴赏力、见多识广的受众；a sophisticated understanding 深刻而成熟的理解；sophisticated tastes 高雅、成熟的品味；a sophisticated argument 周密、复杂的论证。音：/səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd/ adj.","createdAt":1793270897723,"srs":{"ef":2.6,"interval":4,"reps":1,"lapses":0,"due":1793635200000,"lastGrade":5,"lastReview":1793323184667,"history":[{"t":1793323184667,"grade":5,"ivl":4,"ef":2.6}]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"learning","updatedAt":1793323184667},{"id":"wmvtf6wcaldcsc","term":"narrow","key":"narrow","userDef":"义：狭窄的；有限的；狭隘的。不只描述物理宽度，也可描述范围、视野和差距；作动词时表示使变窄、缩小。搭配：a narrow road 狭窄的道路；a narrow margin 微弱的差距；a narrow escape 死里逃生；侥幸脱险；a narrow perspective 狭隘的视角；narrow the gap 缩小差距；narrow one's focus 缩小关注范围；narrow down the options 缩小选择范围。音：/ˈnærəʊ/ adj. & v.","createdAt":1793270897724,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793270897722,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793270897724},{"id":"wmvtf6wcawjtbc","term":"on my mind","key":"on my mind","userDef":"义：某事萦绕心头，让人挂念、担忧或持续思考。例：I have a lot on my mind right now.（我现在有很多事情要操心）Something has been weighing on my mind lately.（最近有件事一直让我心事重重）You seem distracted. What's on your mind?（你似乎心不在焉，在想什么呢）辨：带挂念、忧虑色彩，不等于 in my mind。","createdAt":1793270897725,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793270897722,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793270897725},{"id":"wmvtf6wca0o6ft","term":"in my mind","key":"in my mind","userDef":"义：在我的思想、认知或想象中；强调主观认识或心理图景，相当于 in my opinion（在我看来）。例：In my mind, translation is both an art and a science.（在我看来，翻译既是艺术也是科学）I could still picture the scene in my mind.（我仍能在脑海中想象出那个场景）In my mind, the two concepts are closely related.（在我的理解中，这两个概念密切相关）辨：on my mind 是心里挂着一件事；in my mind 是在脑中思考、想象或认为。","createdAt":1793270897726,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793270897722,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793270897726},{"id":"wmvtf6wcasw9a8","term":"scarcity","key":"scarcity","userDef":"义：缺乏；稀缺。强调某种资源或事物供应不足，尤其是相对于需求而言。搭配：scarcity of resources 资源匮乏；water scarcity 水资源短缺；food scarcity 食物短缺；a scarcity of evidence 证据不足；scarcity of qualified translators 合格译者短缺。音：/ˈskeəsəti/ n.","createdAt":1793270897727,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793270897722,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793270897727},{"id":"wmvtf6wcar1mf5","term":"warfare","key":"warfare","userDef":"义：战争；作战。强调战争或对抗的形式、方式和过程，而不只是某一场具体的战争。搭配：modern warfare 现代战争；psychological warfare 心理战；cyber warfare 网络战；guerrilla warfare 游击战；biological warfare 生物战；economic warfare 经济战。辨：war 指具体的某场战争或战争状态，warfare 指作战方式这一类抽象概念。","createdAt":1793270897728,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793270897722,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793270897728},{"id":"wmvtf6wca76ocw","term":"canon","key":"canon","userDef":"义：正典；经典作品体系；规范。文学研究、翻译研究和文化研究中的重要概念，指被某个文化、学术传统或文学史确认为重要、具有代表性或经典地位的作品集合。搭配：the literary canon 文学经典体系；the Western canon 西方经典作品体系；canonical works 经典作品。音：/ˈkænən/ n.","createdAt":1793270897729,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793270897722,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793270897729},{"id":"wmvtf6wca9x67o","term":"run through","key":"run through","userDef":"义：多义短语动词，意思取决于语境。① 快速浏览、过一遍：Let's run through the main points.（我们快速过一遍要点）② 排练、演练：We ran through the presentation twice.（我们把演示排练了两遍）③ 贯穿、遍布：A river runs through the city.（一条河流穿过这座城市）④ 贯穿始终、反复出现：This theme runs through the novel.（这一主题贯穿整部小说）⑤ 用光、耗尽：He ran through his savings.（他花光了积蓄）⑥ 突然闪过脑海：A thought ran through my mind.（一个念头闪过我的脑海）","createdAt":1793270897730,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793270897722,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793270897730},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm96cks","term":"undertake","key":"undertake","userDef":"义：承担，着手进行；承诺做某事。搭配：undertake a task / project / study 承担任务、项目、研究；undertake to do sth 承诺做某事；undertake responsibility 承担责任。辨：比 take on 正式，多用于研究、调查、工程等需要投入时间精力的事。音：/ˌʌndərˈteɪk/ v.","createdAt":1793279153938,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153938},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmxv3zs","term":"profundity","key":"profundity","userDef":"义：深刻；深奥；深刻的见解。搭配：the profundity of his thought 他思想的深刻性；philosophical profundity 哲学深度。辨：depth 更常用、更宽泛；profundity 更正式，常用于思想、洞见、文学或哲学讨论，不宜泛用于日常的「深」。音：/prəˈfʌndəti/ n.","createdAt":1793279153939,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153939},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm65crx","term":"scholarship","key":"scholarship","userDef":"义：① 学术研究；学术造诣（不可数）。② 奖学金（可数，a scholarship）。例：Her scholarship has made a significant contribution to translation studies.（她的学术研究为翻译学作出了重要贡献）He won a full scholarship to study abroad.（他获得了全额奖学金）辨：两义靠可数性区分，翻译时先看冠词。音：/ˈskɑːlərʃɪp/ n.","createdAt":1793279153940,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153940},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm5lnrr","term":"specimen","key":"specimen","userDef":"义：样本；标本；典型实例；某类人的代表。搭配：a specimen of a rare plant 稀有植物标本；a fine specimen of craftsmanship 精湛工艺的典范；a specimen of humanity 某种类型人类的代表（具体含义取决于语境，常带调侃）。例：He was a fine specimen of the Victorian gentleman.（他堪称维多利亚时代绅士的典型）音：/ˈspesɪmən/ n.","createdAt":1793279153941,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153941},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmmd7tl","term":"generalize","key":"generalize","userDef":"义：概括；归纳；泛化；以偏概全。搭配：generalize from specific cases 从具体案例中归纳；generalize about a group 对某一群体作概括性判断；generalize too broadly 作过于宽泛的概括；generalize from one case 根据一个案例推而广之。辨：中性义是「归纳」，与 too broadly、from one case 连用时才指向以偏概全。音：/ˈdʒenrəlaɪz/ v.","createdAt":1793279153942,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153942},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm8veuq","term":"sweeping","key":"sweeping","userDef":"义：（用于评价、论证）范围过大的；笼统的；未经充分限定的。搭配：a sweeping generalization 以偏概全的笼统概括；a sweeping statement 过于笼统的断言；a sweeping conclusion 过于宽泛的结论；sweeping changes 全面而大幅度的变革（此时不含负面意味）。辨：褒贬取决于所修饰的名词，与 changes、reforms 连用时是中性褒义。音：/ˈswiːpɪŋ/ adj.","createdAt":1793279153943,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153943},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm5m2mk","term":"solid","key":"solid","userDef":"义：扎实的；可靠的；有实际价值的。搭配：a solid achievement 扎实的成就；solid work 扎实、经得起检验的工作；solid evidence 确凿的证据；a solid foundation 坚实的基础；solid progress 切实的进展。辨：评价学术成果时的常用褒词，强调经得起检验而非亮眼。音：/ˈsɑːlɪd/ adj.","createdAt":1793279153944,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153944},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm71uuc","term":"despise","key":"despise","userDef":"义：鄙视；蔑视；看不起。搭配：despise sb for sth 因某事而鄙视某人。辨：语气远强于 dislike，含道德上的轻蔑，主语往往自认站在高处。音：/dɪˈspaɪz/ v.","createdAt":1793279153945,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153945},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm179dk","term":"despicable","key":"despicable","userDef":"义：卑劣的；可鄙的；令人不齿的。搭配：despicable behavior 卑劣的行为；a despicable act 令人不齿的行径。辨：despise 是「看不上某人」，despicable 是「此人此事本身可鄙」，前者是态度，后者是判断。音：/dɪˈspɪkəbəl/ adj.","createdAt":1793279153946,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153946},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmga1ia","term":"rectitude","key":"rectitude","userDef":"义：正直；道德操守；品行端正。搭配：moral rectitude 道德正直。辨：正式书面语，指严格意义上的道德正确；日常口语少用，用时常带一丝戏谑。音：/ˈrektɪtuːd/ n.","createdAt":1793279153947,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153947},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmpcyn1","term":"righteous","key":"righteous","userDef":"义：正义的；正直的；自认为正义的。搭配：a righteous cause 正义的事业；righteous anger 义愤；self-righteous 自以为是的、自命正义的。辨：单独使用多为正面；一旦加上 self- 就转为贬义，指道德优越感。音：/ˈraɪtʃəs/ adj.","createdAt":1793279153948,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153948},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmlyb38","term":"snobbery","key":"snobbery","userDef":"义：势利；势利行为；基于阶层、财富、出身或文化品位而自视高人一等的态度。搭配：intellectual snobbery 知识上的优越感、知识势利；social snobbery 社会势利；cultural snobbery 文化势利。音：/ˈsnɑːbəri/ n.","createdAt":1793279153949,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153949},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm5ivph","term":"mercenary","key":"mercenary","userDef":"义：① 形容词：唯利是图的，以金钱利益为主要动机的。② 名词：雇佣兵。搭配：a mercenary motive 唯利是图的动机；a mercenary attitude 一切向钱看的态度。音：/ˈmɜːrsəneri/ adj. & n.","createdAt":1793279153950,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153950},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm79fpm","term":"materialistic","key":"materialistic","userDef":"义：物质主义的；过分看重金钱、财富和物质享受的。搭配：a materialistic society 物质至上的社会；a materialistic outlook 物质主义的人生观。辨：带贬义，评价的是价值观取向，不是哲学立场。音：/məˌtɪriəˈlɪstɪk/ adj.","createdAt":1793279153951,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153951},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm81ryj","term":"materialism","key":"materialism","userDef":"义：① 消费与价值观语境：物质主义，过分重视财富、消费和物质享受。② 哲学语境：唯物主义，认为物质是世界的基础或本原的哲学立场。例：Consumerism often encourages materialism.（消费主义往往助长物质主义）historical materialism 历史唯物主义。辨：中文有两个译法，必须按语境选，不能一律译作「唯物主义」。音：/məˈtɪriəlɪzəm/ n.","createdAt":1793279153952,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153952},{"id":"wmvtk3uvml0bhy","term":"limelight","key":"limelight","userDef":"义：公众关注；聚光灯下的位置；风头。搭配：be in the limelight 成为公众关注的焦点；step into the limelight 进入公众视野；seek the limelight 追求关注。音：/ˈlaɪmlaɪt/ n.","createdAt":1793279153953,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153953},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm7t6fy","term":"court","key":"court","userDef":"义：① 动词：试图获得；博得；争取。② 求爱；追求。③ 招致（危险、失败等）。搭配：court popularity 博取人气、追求受欢迎；court public opinion 争取公众支持；court disaster 自找麻烦。音：/kɔːrt/ v.","createdAt":1793279153954,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153954},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm0mmpb","term":"put on an air of","key":"put on an air of","userDef":"义：装出……的样子；摆出……的姿态，通常暗示刻意伪装、并不真实。搭配：put on an air of confidence 装出自信的样子；put on an air of indifference 装作无所谓。例：She put on an air of confidence she did not feel.（她装出一副自己并没有的自信）辨：与 assume an air of 意思相近，但 put on 更口语、更强调「装」，assume 偏书面且中性。","createdAt":1793279153955,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153955},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmumr90","term":"assume an air of","key":"assume an air of","userDef":"义：摆出……的姿态；采取某种神态。强调主动采取某种态度或神情。搭配：assume an air of superiority 摆出高人一等的姿态；assume an air of calm 摆出镇定的神态。辨：语气比 put on 中性，不一定暗示虚伪，更像「主动进入某种状态」。","createdAt":1793279153956,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153956},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm1fr4l","term":"strike a pose","key":"strike a pose","userDef":"义：摆出某种姿势；刻意塑造某种形象；也可指摆拍。搭配：strike a pose for the camera 对着镜头摆姿势。辨：偏具体的身体姿态或对外形象，常含做作意味。","createdAt":1793279153957,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153957},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm28esf","term":"adopt an attitude of","key":"adopt an attitude of","userDef":"义：采取某种态度。搭配：adopt an attitude of indifference 采取漠然的态度。辨：adopt 强调主动选择、采纳某种立场，语气中性偏正式，不带表演色彩。","createdAt":1793279153958,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153958},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm9rmjp","term":"strike an attitude of","key":"strike an attitude of","userDef":"义：摆出某种姿态或姿势。通常较正式，也可能带戏剧化或做作的意味。辨：与 adopt an attitude of 相比，strike 更强调做给人看的姿态，adopt 更强调内心立场的选择。","createdAt":1793279153959,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153959},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmq7cmu","term":"look down on","key":"look down on","userDef":"义：看不起；轻视；认为某人低人一等。也写作 look down upon，意思完全相同。搭配：look down on sb for sth 因某事看不起某人。例：He looks down on people who never went to university.（他看不起没上过大学的人）辨：比 despise 语气轻，多指态度上的轻蔑而非道德审判。","createdAt":1793279153960,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153960},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmcg2sf","term":"alike","key":"alike","userDef":"义：相似的；同样地；两者都。常见结构：be alike 相似；look alike 长得相似；treat A and B alike 平等对待 A 和 B；young and old alike 无论年轻人还是老年人。辨：只作表语或副词，不作定语——不说 an alike pair，要用 similar。音：/əˈlaɪk/ adj. & adv.","createdAt":1793279153961,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153961},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmg6doz","term":"ill-advised","key":"ill-advised","userDef":"义：考虑不周的；不明智的；欠妥的。搭配：an ill-advised decision 不明智的决定；an ill-advised remark 欠考虑的言论。辨：反义 well-advised；只评事，不评人。音：/ˌɪl ədˈvaɪzd/ adj.","createdAt":1793279153962,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153962},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmdph2j","term":"worldly-wise","key":"worldly-wise","userDef":"义：老于世故的；深谙人情世故的；懂得现实社会运作规则的。例：Although young, she was surprisingly worldly-wise.（尽管年轻，她却出人意料地深谙世故）辨：中性偏褒，强调经验带来的通透，与 cynical（愤世嫉俗、不再相信善意）不同。音：/ˌwɜːrldli ˈwaɪz/ adj.","createdAt":1793279153963,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153963},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmkzkxj","term":"tactful","key":"tactful","userDef":"义：得体的；圆通的；注意措辞和他人感受的。搭配：a tactful response 得体的回应；be tactful about sth 在某事上注意分寸；tactfully avoid a question 巧妙地避开一个问题。例：She tactfully pointed out the error without embarrassing him.（她得体地指出了错误，没有让他难堪）辨：积极评价，强调善于处理敏感问题；名词是 tact，副词 tactfully。音：/ˈtæktfəl/ adj.","createdAt":1793279153964,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153964},{"id":"wmvtk3uvmcn457","term":"people person","key":"people person","userDef":"义：善于与人相处、喜欢与人打交道的人。例：I'm not really a people person; I prefer working independently.（我其实不太擅长与人打交道，更喜欢独立工作）","createdAt":1793279153965,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153965},{"id":"wmvtk3uvm7h32i","term":"be peopled by","key":"be peopled by","userDef":"义：某个地方、故事或场景中「充满了某类人」或「有某类人物活动其中」。此处 people 是动词，不是名词，也常写作 be peopled with。搭配：be peopled by scholars 有学者活动其中；be peopled with strange characters 充满了奇怪的人物；a novel peopled by memorable characters 一部塑造了许多令人难忘人物的小说。辨：by 侧重「由谁构成」，with 侧重「充满」，多数语境可互换。","createdAt":1793279153966,"srs":{"ef":2.5,"interval":0,"reps":0,"lapses":0,"due":1793279153938,"lastGrade":null,"lastReview":null,"history":[]},"mastered":false,"deleted":false,"status":"new","updatedAt":1793279153966}],"stats":{"days":{"2026-10-29":{"newCount":53,"reviewCount":0,"dev":{"wmvs5y7tttgbc3":{"n":53,"r":0}}},"2026-10-30":{"newCount":11,"reviewCount":9,"dev":{"wmvs5y7tttgbc3":{"n":2,"r":9}}}}},"meta":{"savedAt":1793323215490,"lastExport":0,"deviceId":"wmvs5y7tttgbc3","syncState":"local","settingsAt":1793279093592,"clearedAt":0}}